          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சமூகம் — camūkam — \"society; a community\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஒவ்வொருவரும் சமூகத்துக்கு உதவ வேண்டும். ovvoruvarum camūkattukku utava vēṇṭum. Everyone should help society."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சமூகத்துக்கு, to society, with the oblique -அத்து-. Before another noun, சமூக means social."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சமூகம் (camūkam) is borrowed from Sanskrit samūha, \"heap, collection\" (CDIAL 13241), whose Pali and Prakrit forms mean \"multitude\": people taken together."
            }
          ]
        },
